On Jun 29,  2:14pm, Alan G. Isaac wrote:
> Whitaker responds to the idea that state funded education might be
> a way of enforcing children's rights against their parents by
> suggesting that it is more important for the state to enforce his
> rights to his income. Is this a response?
>
> A subsidiary, implicit theme in his response seems to be that children
> should be viewed as the _property_ of their parents. Why??
>

>Russell Whitaker replied on Wed, 29 Jun 1994 14:21:56:
>From what plane did you pluck _that_ interpretation?  That's truly odd.
